(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-transpile/src/core/asn.asl#" :text "ASN reader and writer in pure AgentSlang. Normative source: docs/ASN_SPEC.md.\n\n  The token stream comes from packages/asl-parser's lexer rather than a second\n  scanner: ASN's whole claim is that it shares AGENT_SPEC_CORE.md section 2's\n  lexical structure, and two scanners would be two answers to what a token is.\n  What is NOT reused is asl-parser's ast.asl reader, which normalises a Nano atom\n  to its verbose spelling: right for a program, wrong for data, because an ASN key\n  spelled :f is a field called f and must survive as one.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-transpile/src/core/asnCheck.asl#" :text "The schema-free half of ASN conformance. Normative source: docs/ASN_SPEC.md sections 11 and 14.\n\n  Only the rules a decoder can decide from the text alone live here. Whether a\n  record inside a row is a sparse override or an ordinary positional value is a\n  question the field count answers, so every row-* rule, nil-at-required-field,\n  unknown-schema and table-missing-column belong to schema-directed\n  materialisation and are deliberately absent rather than guessed at.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-transpile/tests/asnDriver.asl#" :text "Driver for the ASN reader, writer and checker. Every entry answers with text\n      a test can compare against a value written by hand.")
